# ========== PRIVACY STACK: PROJECT MANAGEMENT ==========

# Focalboard - Asana/Trello replacement
# NOTE: upstream (mattermost/focalboard) is unmaintained as a standalone
# project (no releases since 2024, README says "seeking maintainers").
# It still runs fine, but there will be no further security patches.
# Consider Vikunja as a maintained alternative if this matters to you.
boards.{$DOMAIN} {
  import security_headers
  import rate_limit boards
  reverse_proxy focalboard:8000 {
    header_up X-Real-IP {http.request.remote}
  }
}

# ========== PRIVACY STACK: CALENDAR/CONTACTS ==========

# Radicale - CalDAV/CardDAV server. Runs with RADICALE_AUTH_TYPE=none
# (privacy-stack/docker-compose.yml) - Radicale's own auth is disabled
# entirely, not just defaulted, so anyone reaching this hostname could
# read/write every family member's calendar and contacts with zero
# credentials. Caddy-level basic_auth closes that; CalDAV/CardDAV clients
# (phone Calendar/Contacts apps) handle a Basic-auth challenge from a
# fronting proxy exactly the same as one from the CalDAV server itself -
# this is standard, unremarkable behavior for those protocols, not a
# workaround. One shared family credential (distinct from the arr-apps
# one above), since this is genuinely family-facing rather than admin-only.
cal.{$DOMAIN} {
  import security_headers
  basic_auth {
    {$RADICALE_AUTH_USER} {$RADICALE_AUTH_HASH}
  }
  reverse_proxy radicale:5232 {
    header_up X-Real-IP {http.request.remote}
  }
}

